omx-panel (0.13.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: build the DEBs beside the RPMs
  * packaging: the renderer ships as a shared library, per architecture
  * Release 0.13.0
  * meaning-infer: a CLAP parameter's band is read from its name
  * describe: the inference completes an EQ band the words name with its Q,
    type and switch
  * describe: a CLAP feature a scan spells by its macro is the feature it
    stands for
  * renderer: a shared library for a surface that loads it at run time;
    describe --layout gives the layout it draws
  * workflows: run in Open-Mixer while FreeMixer is restricted
  * workflows: run in Open-Mixer while FreeMixer is restricted
  * workflows: run in Open-Mixer while FreeMixer is restricted
  * ci: packaging runs on v* tags and workflow_dispatch only
  * ci: cancel a pull request's stale runs
  * omx-complement-sync: --check names where MODGUI_DIR stands on the list,
    and the default list puts it first (#153)
  * renderer: one recorded meter stream measured on the renderer, in Chromium
    and in Tk
  * MOD GUI: the meter frame is styled without a curve; the pedal rim takes
    no layout
  * renderer: the meter's marker is omx-dsp's omx_meter_view_step
  * The renderer and the MOD GUI draw the description's meters
  * describe: every meter row names its section; a camelCase in and out level
    is the curve's operating point
  * docs: a meter carries measurement, held and clip; a foreign meter guesses
    none
  * describe reads the descriptor's meters word
  * codes: omx-panel's refusals are panel.<group>.<reason> codes
  * Foreign meters stop guessing their measurement from the unit
  * codes: the source sentence beside the code, Catalan in catalogs/ca.json
  * look-roles: name the spec by its title, not its private file name
  * omx-panel: a refusal prints its code and the owner's en sentence,
    placeholders filled
  * look: derive look.json and the renderer's role list from the roles;
    tokens.css goes
  * codes: the 30 codes omx-panel emits carry en and ca text in
    schema/codes.json
  * look-roles: declare the panel's colour roles once, and the tests that
    read them
  * test: every code omx-panel emits carries en and ca text in one codes file
  * package-lock: omx-contract 3.11.0, the new floor
  * skin-package: en and ca text for every refusal code (omx-contract#206)

